call_any_api_of_docstar: inputSchema  parameters: -in; +in, or only the scheme the docs put before the token, e.g. "Bearer" for "Authorization: Bearer <token>";
call_any_read_api_of_docstar: inputSchema  parameters: -in; +in, or only the scheme the docs put before the token, e.g. "Bearer" for "Authorization: Bearer <token>";
send_feedback_to_docstar: description, inputSchema, annotations  -Sends +Send -straight +about Docstar -DocStar team. +team that maintains it: a bug, something missing or wrong in the docs, a feature request, or praise. -wants +asks -a bug, request a feature, flag wrong -missing docs, +suggest something, -share praise about DocStar +when the docs -this MCP server. +the API clearly didn't do what they say. -in +so the team can act on it without the conversation: what was tried, what happened, what was expected. Never include tokens, passwords, API keys or -words and add any useful context, such as the tool or endpoint involved and what went wrong. Who sent i  parameters: -input.collectionId input.collectionId +input.contact_email input.contact_email -e.g. RoNWaspA9p3Z input.context input.context description: e.g. {"tool":"get_docstar_mcp_api_docs"} +The user's email, only if they asked to be contacted about it -e.g. get_api_docs didn't list +The feedback itself, up to 5000 characters input.page_or_endpoint input.page_or_endpoint description: The docs page URL or -MCP Server module's new endpoints +endpoint (e.g. POST /v1/messages) it is about, if any -e.g. bug +What kind of feedback it is input.type enum: ["bug", "docs", "feature_request", "praise", "other"]
